description:
Design a combinational logic circuit that processes a 3-bit input (`v_in`) to produce a 3-bit output (`v_out`). The output bits are determined by specific logical operations on the input bits: the first output is true if either (v_in[2] and v_in[0]) or (v_in[1] and v_in[0]) are true; the second output is true if v_in[2] is true and v_in[1] is false; the third output is true if both v_in[2] and v_in[1] are true. This circuit effectively implements a custom logic function based on the input combinations.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] v_in,
    output [2:0] v_out
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] v_in,
    output [2:0] v_out
    );assign v_out[0] = (v_in[2] & v_in[0]) | (v_in[1] & v_in[0]); 
	assign v_out[1] = (v_in[2] & ~v_in[1]);
	assign v_out[2] = (v_in[2] & v_in[1]);

endmodule

