Design a four-bit adder that computes the sum of two 4-bit inputs, A and B. The output, Y, is a 5-bit result to accommodate potential overflow from the addition, with the most significant bit representing the carry-out. The module utilizes a series of combinational logic gates to perform the addition and generate the appropriate carry outputs between each bit addition.
