description:
Design a circuit that operates as a Muller gate, specifically the 3-input variant. It takes four inputs: 'a', 'p', 'n', and 'rstn'. The output 'z' is set to LOW when 'rstn' is LOW, effectively resetting the output. When 'rstn' is HIGH, 'z' becomes HIGH if both 'a' and 'p' are HIGH. Alternatively, 'z' will be LOW if 'a' is LOW and 'n' is also LOW. This design performs logical operations based on the specified conditions, allowing it to function as a control mechanism in digital circuits.
module top_module(

   z,

   a, p, n, rstn
   );

code:
module top_module(

   z,

   a, p, n, rstn
   );input  a;
  input  p;
  input  n;
  input  rstn;
  output z;



  reg                   z;


  always @* begin
    if(rstn == 1'b0) begin
      z <= 0;
    end
    else begin
      if((a==1'b1) & (p==1'b1)) begin
        z <= #1 1'b1;
      end
      else if((a==1'b0) & (n==1'b0)) begin
         z <= #1 1'b0;
      end
    end

  end



endmodule

