description:
Design a traffic light controller that orchestrates the cycling of traffic lights between red, green, and yellow states. The module accepts a clock and reset signal, with an internal counter managing state transitions every 10 clock cycles. The output light_status represents the current state of the traffic light, with the specific encoding indicating whether the light is red, green, or off. Upon reset, the system initializes to the red light state, ensuring a predictable start condition. This design effectively manages the timing and sequence of traffic lights to regulate vehicle flow at an intersection.
