description:
Design a 32-bit right shift module that takes a 32-bit input and a 5-bit shift amount. The module performs a logical right shift operation on the input based on the specified shift amount, filling the vacated bits with zeros. The output is a 32-bit value resulting from this shift operation, effectively shifting the input bits to the right while ensuring that any new bits introduced on the left are set to zero.
module top_module(
  input [31:0] in,
  input [4:0] shift,
  output [31:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [31:0] in,
  input [4:0] shift,
  output [31:0] out
);// Create a temporary wire to hold the shifted input
  wire [31:0] shifted_input;

  // Perform the right shift operation
  assign shifted_input = in >> shift;

  // Fill the shifted-in bits with zeros
  assign out = shifted_input & ((1 << 32) - (1 << shift));

endmodule

